-- title:
--   Tuple Interpolated Vertical Line Eq Of No Supported Mismatch
-- statement:
--   **A vertical line matching every supported slice is the interpolated line.** Let $u$ be a point, let $\mathbf x$ be an injective point tuple, let $\mathbf g$ be an interpolation-eligible G-hat outcome tuple, and let $f$ be an axis-line polynomial. Assume no supported completed entry of $\mathbf g$ disagrees with $f$ at the corresponding point of $\mathbf x$. If $\mathcal V(u,\mathbf x,\mathbf g)$ denotes the tuple-interpolated vertical line, then
--
--   $$
--   \mathcal V(u,\mathbf x,\mathbf g)=f.
--   $$
--
--   Injectivity and eligibility ensure that interpolation is defined on the selected slices. This is the exact agreement step used to convert supported slice answers into the vertical-line answer.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.tupleInterpolatedVerticalLine_eq_of_no_supported_mismatch`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
